glmark2-mali-tally: causes of oom (main `099b5df6`): 7

## Draft issue 1

Title: gpu-mali: glmark2-es2 build use-vbo=false on the NanoPC-T6: oom: mali: the OSAL refused a buffer of # bytes (#)

Cause 1: oom: mali: the OSAL refused a buffer of # bytes (#)

The first glmark2-es2 run on the NanoPC-T6 (Mali-G610, panthor, back end gpu-mali, #20) from main `099b5df6` (kernel 6.18.55-current-rockchip64, the tools/mali/panthor-gles pair, libGLESv2.so.2 sha256 `3f6c0a1d9e2b4c5a`), one glmark2-es2 process per scene at 800x600 on an EGL pbuffer, gives verdict oom in 1 scene(s): `[build] use-vbo=false`.

- `[build] use-vbo=false`: exit 0, timeout 0, panthor kernel lines 0; 2.08 ms a frame
  > mali: the OSAL refused a buffer of 7684096 bytes (-12)
  > yakogl-mali-exit: draws=4800 refused=0 first_refused=- gpu_faults=0 job_timeouts=0

Run directory `oom`, tallied by `tools/cts/glmark2-mali-tally.py`. Rerun the scene alone with tools/cts/mali-glmark2-run.sh to reproduce. ROADMAP.md stage 2 asks for all 33 scenes with no failed scene, no GL error and no scene out of GPU memory.

